From 4aebeaa1b129ac970e061461633847dfd1d2aa3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Li Jinpei <jinpli@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:51:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [CodeGen][debug-only] Tag COPY/MOV instructions with their
 creating pass

Not for upstream. Behind the hidden -copy-origin flag (default off; no
codegen change), a side table records for each COPY and MOV instruction
the pass that created it (tagged after every MachineFunctionPass), with
details from PHI elimination (PHI, block, incoming edge), two-address
lowering (tied operand / REG_SEQUENCE / INSERT_SUBREG) and greedy
SplitKit (split strategy). ExpandPostRAPseudos and CloneMachineInstr
carry tags to the emitted moves, and AsmPrinter prints them as
'origin:' comments.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
